# add git-ignore syntax here of things you don't want copied into docker image

.git
*Dockerfile*
*docker-compose*
node_modules
node_modules/

# SECURITY: local-proxy/proxy.env holds the OpenSearch credentials. Without
# this, `docker build` copies it into the build context and bakes it into an
# image layer, where anyone with the image can recover it via `docker history`
# or by extracting the layer. In production the credential comes from a
# Kubernetes Secret at runtime instead -- see deploy/README.md.
local-proxy/
*.env
!*.env.example

# Local build output and editor noise -- never wanted in the image
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local dev config. The image bakes deploy/config/*.prod.js over these instead,
# so a developer's localhost settings cannot leak into a deployed bundle and the
# build does not depend on untracked files.
src/config/index.js
src/config/tosca.js
src/config/figaro.js

# Our own notes and scratch files
HYSDS_UI_SETUP_NOTES.md
